    "data": "Eight packed f64 values per row; seeded finite corpus plus signed-zero, exact-boundary and finite-magnitude edge cases",
    "parity": "Object.is for every scalar and batch result, preserving signed zero; inputs checked unchanged; zero-count batch checked",
    "performance": "1024 seeded rows; warmup; shared power-of-two pass calibration to at least 12 ms for both candidates; fifteen samples with alternating JS/Wasm order; exact checksums; no wall-time CI gate",
    "batchCopies": "Each timed Wasm batch includes 64 bytes per row copied into linear memory, one boundary call, 8 bytes per row copied back to a JavaScript Float64Array, and the same output checksum loop used by JS. Typed-array views and memory allocation are outside timing.",
    "limitations": [
      "Favorable Wasm lower bound: inputs are already packed; extracting existing Velocity/Vector3 objects, material/profile resolution, packing and application to engine objects are not modeled.",
      "Only an isolated arithmetic scalar and boundary/copies are measured. No collision, AI, replay, audio, rendering, complete movement update or Simulation.step port is benchmarked.",
      "Rust and a Rust-generated module are unmeasured; there is no installed Rust/Cargo/Clang/Wasm optimizer toolchain.",
